"When he went through so many things at such a young age - he went to the first Olympics at the age of fourteen and his father died of cancer three years later - he said it was hard to find a brother-in-law who had gone through a similar agony.
The couple became the parents of their son, called Robert Ray Black, in June, and Daley said his "frontal perspective" had changed.
“When I asked him last year, he said, ‘You’ve got to win a gold medal.’
“It’s bigger than an Olympic gold medal.
“My Olympic gold medal is Robbie.”
His son has the same name as his father Robert, who passed away at the age of forty after being diagnosed with a brain tumour.
Daley said his father didn’t accept that he was going to die, and one of the last things he asked for was whether they still had a ticket to London in 2012 because he wanted to be in the front row.
