“Unlike the previous president, who had a formal question-and-answer session, President Trump will discuss the matter honestly,” he said, adding, “We’re looking at the figures without providing any specific evidence.”
"Wouldn't it be much better if reporters had the opportunity to ask the president of the United States directly instead of me?
“The White House is trying to have a lot of opportunities, and we’ve actually had a conversation over the last few weeks, and even at press briefings, we’re going to let journalists talk directly with the President of the United States,” Sanders added.
