Fallu is the capital of the central part of Sulawesi, at the end of a narrow bay on the west coast of Sulawesi Island, with a population of about 379,800 as of 2017.
Fallu was hit by earthquakes and tsunamis as it celebrated its 40th anniversary of the city's founding.
Donggala is a regency region that stretches 300km (180miles) along the coast of the northwest region of Sulawesi.
The regency area is one administrative level below the province's population, with a population of about 299,200 as of 2017.
Agriculture and fishing are the main industries in central Sulawesi, especially in the Donggala region.
